From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:44:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: m4: end an external DCP's PM epoch when
 its stop fails

aurora-silicon/linux#1314's rewrite of "drm/apple: m4: stop the
external DCPs for a deep sleep and restart them": the PM core resumes
no device whose suspend failed, so a failed stop flushes the RTKit
receive queue and ends the sleep's PM epoch itself, as resume would.
Otherwise no later powerUpDART counts as fresh and the output stays
dark.

This applies the rewrite's change to the revision k881 carries.

Based on 72065ad011 from aurora-silicon/linux#1314.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
index 0d36265917..e589002a5a 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
@@ -8362,6 +8362,16 @@ int iomfb_m4_suspend(struct apple_dcp *owner)
 				ret = dcp->gated ? apple_dart_cio_gated(dcp->ext_darts[1]) : 0;
 		}
 		mutex_unlock(&dcp->lock);
+		/*
+		 * The PM core resumes no device whose suspend failed: end the
+		 * sleep's epoch here, as resume would, or no later powerUpDART
+		 * counts as fresh and the output stays dark.
+		 */
+		if (ret) {
+			if (dcp->rtkit)
+				apple_rtkit_flush_rx(dcp->rtkit);
+			atomic_inc(&dcp->ext_pm_epoch);
+		}
 		return ret;
 	}
 	if (!dcp || !dcp->runtime)
